	<annotations>
		<text id="0" type="text/plain" rect="(20.0, 20.0, 560.0, 82.0)" font-family="Helvetica" font-size="13">PRAKTIKUM 4 — Inference

Orange is a visual tool, not a statistics package. It shows association clearly
(Sieve, Mosaic, Distributions) and defers the formal test to the Python Script.</text>
		<text id="1" type="text/plain" rect="(620.0, 200.0, 340.0, 210.0)" font-family="Helvetica" font-size="13">WHAT TO DO
1. Distributions: 'converted', split by 'variant'.
   Eyeball the difference -- is it convincing?
2. Box Plot: 'session_seconds' by 'variant'. Orange
   prints a t-test at the bottom of this widget.
3. Sieve Diagram: variant x converted. The colour
   shows the deviation from independence.
4. SIMPSON CHECK: Mosaic with variant, converted
   AND device. Does the lift hold in both devices?
5. Python Script: paste the snippet from the book
   (section 4.8.2) to get z, p and the CI.</text>
	</annotations>
